' PAL — State diagram for UC-06: Payment lifecycle
@startuml PAL_State_UC06_Payment

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #444
skinparam StateBackgroundColor #FDF6E3
skinparam StateBorderColor #333
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF8DC
skinparam NoteBorderColor #888
hide empty description

title UC-06 — Payment state machine\n(rental fee + deposit; Booking is created as a side-effect on capture)

[*] --> Pending : / submit charge to gateway

Pending : do / wait for gateway response
Pending --> Captured : gateway confirms success\n/ create Booking(PaidPickupPending),\n  notify lender, show Borrowing detail
Pending --> Failed   : gateway rejects\n/ show error to borrower
Pending --> Pending  : gateway timeout\n/ mark reconcile async (alt 5b)

Failed --> Pending : borrower retries\nwith different method (alt 5a)
Failed --> [*]     : borrower abandons\nafter N retries

Captured --> Refunded : cancellation (UC-09)\nor dispute resolution\n/ refund via gateway
Captured --> [*]      : booking settled normally\n(no refund needed)

Refunded --> [*]

note right of Pending
  Self-transition (Pending → Pending) represents
  UC-06 alt 5b: the Payment row stays in Pending
  while async reconciliation runs against the gateway.
end note

note bottom of Captured
  Side-effects of the
  Pending → Captured transition:
   • Booking created in state PaidPickupPending
   • Lender notified
   • Borrowing detail screen shown to borrower
  (Cross-UC: feeds UC-07 handover.)
end note

note left of Refunded
  Cross-UC edge from UC-09:
  refund amount is computed by the
  cancellation policy in UC-09.
end note

@enduml
